EXT. ROOFTOP OF A DEFUNCT BOWLING ALLEY - NIGHT

A flat tar roof with a giant fiberglass bowling pin tilted at one corner. Orange glow of a distant highway. Six teenagers sit in a rough circle around a dying cooler.

MAYA OSEI (17, braids, denim jacket) holds the last warm soda. LUCAS BRANDÃO (17, skinny, borrowed varsity jacket) fiddles with a lighter. TILLIE VANCE (16, hair dyed green, headphones round her neck) lies flat on her back. DARIUS PEÑA-OKAFOR (18, quiet, a duffel at his feet). ROSALIE MAHMOUD (17, glasses, scholarship folder under her arm) sits cross-legged. And FINN ASHWORTH-DIOP (16, the youngest, hoodie sleeves over his hands) has pulled his knees to his chin.

Darius stands. Lucas tracks him with the lighter flame. Tillie sits up on one elbow. Maya turns her head. Rosalie closes her folder. Finn pulls the sleeves further down. Darius lifts the duffel and slings it over his shoulder as if it were weightless.

DARIUS
(to everyone)
So, that's it. Bus is at six.

TILLIE
Six in the morning?

DARIUS
Yeah.

TILLIE
That's, like, five hours.

DARIUS
Yeah.

MAYA
You said next week.

DARIUS
I said I'd tell you when I knew. Now I know.

Lucas clicks the lighter shut.

LUCAS
That's messed up, man.

DARIUS
Luc.

LUCAS
No, it is. You get a whole summer's notice and you give us five hours?

DARIUS
I didn't want it to be a thing.

ROSALIE
It's a thing.

Finn rubs his eye with a sleeve. Nobody sees except Tillie.

TILLIE
(low, to Finn)
You good?

FINN
(muttering)
I'm fine. Dust.

TILLIE
There's no dust. It's a roof.

Darius sets the duffel down again. He walks to the giant bowling pin at the corner and leans against it, looking out at the highway.

DARIUS
You can all come to the bus.

MAYA
We're coming to the bus.

LUCAS
Obviously we're coming to the bus.

ROSALIE
I'll bring snacks.

Silence. Then Tillie sits up, takes her headphones off her neck, and holds one earbud out to Darius across the circle.

TILLIE
Come listen to something stupid with me.

Darius hesitates. Then crosses the roof and sits beside her. She puts the bud in his ear. Maya leans on Rosalie. Lucas lights the lighter again and holds it up like a concert, and one by one, they all pretend not to be crying.
